nd pull requests for checks you want added."}]]}]]}],["$","div","1",{"children":[["$","details","Is this affiliated with Intuit?",{"open":false,"children":[["$","summary",null,{"children":"Is this affiliated with Intuit?"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"No. It’s an independent open-source project by Apideck. Intuit hasn’t endorsed or reviewed it. Our summary of the requirements is our reading of Intuit’s public documentation and may lag behind changes."}]]}],["$","details","What does the live scan send to my app?",{"open":false,"children":[["$","summary",null,{"children":"What does the live scan send to my app?"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"About 30 ordinary requests: a few GETs, a TRACE, TRACK and OPTIONS, a test call to your OAuth callback with fake parameters, and redirect probes with a harmless test URL. Plus four TLS handshakes. Only scan apps you own or are authorized to test."}]]}],["$","details","Why might it flag code that’s fine?",{"open":false,"children":[["$","summary",null,{"children":"Why might it flag code that’s fine?"}],["$","p",null,{"children":["The source scan uses patterns, so it reports things to review, like an ",["$","code",null,{"children":"innerHTML"}]," that only ever renders static text. Treat warnings as prompts to look, and failures as likely problems to confirm."]}]]}],["$","details","Do I need to keep checking after approval?",{"open":false,"children":[["$","summary",null,{"children":"Do I need to keep checking after approval?"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Listed apps can be reviewed again later, so run the GitHub Action on deploys and on a schedule. A changed header or a new logging line then shows up in CI first."}]]}]]}]]}]]}]}]
